invariant: INV-17
file: sha512_compress_blocks.h
catches: sha2_equiv_test
reason: SHA512_COMPRESS_BLOCKS_BELOW_LEN, the bytes of stack sha512.c wipes
  below each compression call, is 64, less than the frame
  sha512_compress_blocks writes, so the wipe runs and still leaves the
  message schedule's words where they lay. Every digest is right.
  bin/sha2_equiv_test measures how far below its caller the function
  writes and requires that inside the length, and then requires no word a
  call computed in the stack below it.

--- old
#define SHA512_COMPRESS_BLOCKS_BELOW_LEN 512
--- new
#define SHA512_COMPRESS_BLOCKS_BELOW_LEN 64
